  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on 18 July 2002 the erection of a rear extension with a bedroom 4.0m long, 3.8m wide and a maximum height of 3 m and a bathroom 2.6m long, 3.0m wide and a maximum height of 3 m would have been lawful within the meaning of sections 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended) for the following reason;\r\n\r\nThe proposed development would fall within Class A Part 1 Schedule 2 of the Town and Country Planning General Permitted Development Order 1995 because the cubic content of the resulting building would exceed the cubic content of the original dwelling house by more than 70 cubic metres.\r\n\r\nINFORMATIVE\r\nPlanning permission is not required\r\n"
